    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0713" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 612.119/644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-28T15:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 28, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>652. <hi rendition="#italic">El Universal</hi> recently has claimed repeatedly
                    that the Mexican food commission sent to the United States failed utterly; that
                    no corn is being shipped to Mexico. Although this denied by other local papers,
                    public appears to be in doubt as to the real situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
